### Description

In an `isolated class`, a field with default (module) visibility that is mutable, or that is `final` but has a non-readonly type, is accepted. Code outside the class can then read and mutate the object's state without a lock. Only `public` fields are rejected today (`public final int[] parr = [];` correctly gives "public field of an isolated object must be "final" and have a type that is a subtype of "readonly"").

Spec §8.6 ([class definition](https://ballerina.io/spec/lang/master/#section_8.6)): "An object-field or method-defn occurring as a class-member in an isolated class is subject to same requirements as when it occurs as an object-member in an object-constructor-expr that is explicitly isolated."
Spec §6.8.1 (object constructor, isolated objects): "An object field is isolated if it is declared as final and has a type-descriptor that is a subtype of readonly or isolated object {} ... If the object-constructor-expr is explicitly isolated, then every field-initializer must be an isolated expression and any field that is not isolated must be declared as private."

`int count` is not final and `final int[] items` has a non-readonly type, so neither is isolated, and both must be `private`. Expected: compile errors on the two marked lines. Actual: compiles, runs and prints `5`.

Likely cause: `validateIsolatedClassField` (`semantics/internal/analysis/classes.go`) checks `field.IsPublic()` instead of `!field.IsPrivate()`.

### Steps to Reproduce

```ballerina
import ballerina/io;

isolated class Counter {
    int count = 0; // @error non-private mutable field in isolated class
    final int[] items = []; // @error non-private final field whose type is not readonly
    private int total = 0;

    isolated function bump() {
        lock {
            self.total += 1;
        }
    }
}

public function main() {
    Counter c = new;
    c.count = 5;
    c.items.push(1);
    io:println(c.count);
}
```

### Affected Version(s)

`main` @ `00d6965be`

### OS, DB, other environment details and versions

Linux, built from source (`go run ./cli/cmd run <file.bal>`)

### Related area

Semantics

### Related issue(s) (optional)

#1432 and #1431 touch the same isolated-field check (the opposite direction: too strict for final isolated-object fields).

